//! The Rust side of rustyfiles for macOS. The Swift app (`macos/`) calls into it through
//! UniFFI; the bindings are generated by `macos/build.sh`.
//!
//! A folder listing stays in Rust: the table asks for one row at a time ([`Folder::item`]), so
//! a 100,000-item folder never crosses the FFI as one big array, and re-sorting only shuffles
//! an index vector. Formatting (sizes, dates, kinds, icons) is left to the Swift side, where
//! the system formatters make it look the way Finder does.

